<speech id="uk.org.publicwhip/westminhall/2014-05-08a.154.1" speakerid="uk.org.publicwhip/member/40374" speakername="Graeme Morrice" colnum="154"  time="014:48:00" url="http://www.publications.parliament.uk/pa/cm201314/cmhansrd/cm140508/halltext/140508h0001.htm#140508h0001.htm_spnew66">
	<p pid="a.154.1/1">The right hon. Lady talks about the cost. Does she not accept that the evidence provided to the Committee by various witnesses from Scotland and beyond&#8212;all the housing providers, welfare rights organisations, tenants, local authorities and even the Convention of Scottish Local Authorities&#8212;says that the cap is costing everybody more money than it is saving? How does the Minister respond to that, and particularly to the COSLA figure, supported by all political parties in Scotland, that in Scotland it is costing an additional &#163;60 million to administer?</p>
</speech>
